'' A field declaration must end its line -- fbc's error 3, and its error 14 for the
'' type-first spelling whose declarator never arrives. Asserted BY POSITION: an
'' assertion on the id alone would pass with the wrong token blamed.
''
'' The four bad fields are in four TYPEs because the parser reports ONE diagnostic per
'' statement and a whole TYPE body is one -- so a second bad field in the same body is
'' deliberately not reported.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/field-decl-end-of-line.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1

'' 'b as ubyte( 0 to 3 )' -- the bounds belong before the 'as'.
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-decl-end-of-line.bas(21,15): error TKO0420

'' 'b as ubyte junk' -- the same rule over a word rather than a paren.
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-decl-end-of-line.bas(26,16): error TKO0420

'' 'as long a junk' -- and in the type-first spelling too.
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-decl-end-of-line.bas(31,15): error TKO0420

'' 'as ubyte( 0 to 3 ) b' -- no declarator was read at all, which is fbc's error 14.
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-decl-end-of-line.bas(36,13): error TKO0406

'' AND NOTHING OVER THE LEGAL SHAPES in 'type Ok': the bounds before the 'as', a
'' fixed-length string, a procedure pointer's parameter list, a field default, a
'' bitfield width and the comma list. Four diagnostics, no more.
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 4
'' GOLDEN: expected/field-decl-end-of-line.out
